---
import { ClassmapDemo } from '../components/Islands'
import { CacheGame, RackSolver } from '../components/Toys'
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { pageOf, url } from '../lib/data'
---
<Base title="Play · Joshua Bugarin" description="Two toys made from Joshua Bugarin's projects, and one real map: be the cache, search a rack of tiles, walk across campus." current="play">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Play · page {pageOf('play')}</p>
      <h1>Two toys and a map.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Each toy is a small model of one idea from a project. The real numbers are in the case studies.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="toy" id="cache">
      <div class="toy-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">From Pacer</p>
        <h2>Be the cache.</h2>
        <p class="muted">You have four slots. Requests arrive one at a time, and a request for a block you still hold is a hit. When the cache is full and something new arrives, you pick what to throw out. At the end you are scored against two simple rules and against perfect foresight.</p>
        <a class="link" href={url('work/pacer/')}>How Pacer makes this choice</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mat-panel try"><CacheGame client:visible /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="toy" id="rack">
      <div class="toy-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">From TileLens</p>
        <h2>Find the best play.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Seven tiles and a word list. The page finds the highest-scoring words the rack can spell, and times the search.</p>
        <a class="link" href={url('work/tilelens/')}>How TileLens reads a whole board</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mat-panel try"><RackSolver client:visible /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="toy" id="map">
      <div class="toy-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">From Classmap</p>
        <h2>Walk across campus.</h2>
        <p class="muted">This one is not a toy. It is the web map the Classmap repo builds, running in this page.</p>
        <a class="link" href={url('work/classmap/')}>How Classmap finds the room</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mat-panel try"><ClassmapDemo client:visible /></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
